WEBVTT

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.420
Ever since the waterworks incident,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.150
it seems like everyone's in a heavy mood.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:15.780
In particular...

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.780
...the corporal's mood being the heaviest...

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:25.790
I guess...

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.960
...I must do something about this!

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:43.760
So basically,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:49.580
I thought about a lovely dance that everyone can sing and dance to and become happy together with!

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.920
I'll call it Plan A - "Lunatic Dance"!

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:59.030
I spent all morning producing this dance, and I put a lot of effort into it.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.410
And, because people might be concerned that it would be "too embarrassing",

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:09.790
I have decided to test dance it in this experimental area.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:16.470
Here goes.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.760
Pu-Pu-Pu-Pumpkin

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.130
La-La-La-Pumpkin

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:33.730
Scissors...

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.360
Scissors!

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.450
Ah, here goes!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.480
Be it love or battle, how you start is crucial.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:45.220
Dash with all you've got!

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.650
With a cute little move,

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:50.380
Catch the heart!

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:53.330
Catch and release!

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.030
Th-That was much more embarrassing than I anticipated...

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.670
Let's seal this thing away forever.

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:19.990
I-I-I-I-It's not like that!

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:21.640
It's not like that, Corporal!

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.900
There's a reason for this.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:23.620
Corporal!

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.220
No, no, no, no, don't look at me with those eyes!

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.040
Don't close the door!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.010
No, I'm not...

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.230
Everyone has freedom of religion.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.210
At 1310,

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.220
Plan A...

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.050
...sunk.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.610
Continuing on with Plan B!

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.960
"Ask Men About Men" plan!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.690
Begin!

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.750
So, give me some advice.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.610
Huh?

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.130
Just leave him alone.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:04.990
Shhh.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.530
Your voice is too loud.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.850
What exactly is this all about?

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.390
For the sake of the corporal,

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:13.400
as his superior, I thought I should help him out.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.570
Perhaps I can proceed with Plan B?

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.130
Plan B?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.120
I'm just talking to myself.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.380
Besides, why me?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.680
How bothersome.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.550
Because Oreld, you're someone who enjoys the good life.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.470
No one else can make themself enjoy life more than you, Oreld.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.630
Yes, Oreld does live at his own pace.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:40.600
Yes, so please let me in on your secrets of how to please oneself.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.720
Hey, big guy.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.410
Come with me for a bit.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.970
Yes, sir.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:48.980
To where?

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.710
A store to "energize" ourselves.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:51.600
Ahh.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.620
Yes, yes!

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.050
Stores that energize you; the more the better!

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:57.070
Great idea, Oreld.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.170
It paid off asking you about this.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.550
A store that energizes you?

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.940
Yes, one that works for any man.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.250
Right?

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.260
N-NO, NO, BIG NO!

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.530
At 1330,

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.100
Plan B...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:20.730
...blew up!

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.200
Gosh!

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.480
Oreld, you sexually harass me too much!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.360
Do you even understand what sexual harassment means?

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.630
Sexual harassment!

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:30.180
Go home already, would ya?
Sexual harassment!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.210
Go home already, would ya?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.300
Why you!!!

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.380
Now, now, calm down.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.500
He...

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.510
For crying out loud...

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:43.920
What?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.260
Oh yeah, Machs.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.180
Asking Oreld for advice was probably the wrong step to begin with.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:54.990
In that regard, Machs is many times better than me at work,

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.300
and he has a good reputation:

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.680
the perfect person to ask for advice.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:03.420
Seeing him take care of many tasks all by himself

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.650
is a stark contrast to Oreld's enjoyment.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.440
Yes, if I had to put it...

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.090
You're a one-man machine!

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.250
TLNote: Stekkin doesn't realize "Hitorijouzu" also means "masturbation".

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.430
Machs is the Empire's number one one-man machine!

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:21.360
TLNote: Stekkin doesn't realize "Hitorijouzu" also means "masturbation".

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:22.330
Huh?

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.670
The mood's so heavy...

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.160
Nevermind the big guy,

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.430
you're responsible for making Machs like that!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.220
Excuse me.

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.400
Umm, Corporal-

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.000
I don't know...
Umm, Corporal-

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.100
I don't know...

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.990
I don't know what you did in those sewers,

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.910
but you accomplished your mission,

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.490
and we destroyed the Himmel distribution network.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.890
What are you not happy with?

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.580
One-man machine...

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.960
Not you!

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.130
There were people that I couldn't save, as well.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.910
How many...

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:23.320
How many people do you have to save to satisfy your standards, Corporal?!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:26.180
Oreld...

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.610
Looky here...

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:31.610
What a pathetic argument that's going on here.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.030
Section III again?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.380
Hey, Lahn.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.900
What does the great Section I want from us?

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:41.350
Don't worry.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.370
They're not part of Claymore One.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:49.640
Indeed, I wasn't able to qualify for Claymore One.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.830
But, behold!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:56.070
This "Double Shotel" team emblem!

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:01.430
We penetrate the enemy defenses with our superior intelligence.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.080
Our slash is just like that of a shotel!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.670
The sting of a bee!

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.790
The heroes of intelligence warfare!

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:08.090
Do you know him?

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.310
Ah, but that was a very tough six months of training.
Do you know him?

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.360
We were in the same year at the academy.
Ah, but that was a very tough six months of training.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:12.820
By the way,

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.680
was that loud shout from you, Oreld?

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:17.520
Section III sure is lucky,

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.220
all peaceful and easy-going,

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:23.870
while we're on missions fighting for the prestige of the Empire every day.

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:26.370
War relief, was it?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.710
Have you saved like five or ten people now?

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:31.980
Oreld?

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.640
Let's move to another seat.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.710
Running away?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:36.900
Oh, come on.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.190
Does Section III have no guts or what?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.530
Finishing move!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.070
Pumpkin Scissors!!!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.500
Why you!

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.810
I won't allow you to pick on the weak!

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.020
Hold it!

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:04.130
Am I the weak one you refer to?

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:06.740
And... was our team name the name of a move?

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.630
Wh-What?

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.010
I'm sorry.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:15.480
I didn't know that you'd be so depressed, Oreld.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:18.710
The Sergeant Major?

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.140
Well, let's put Oreld aside.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:21.640
Hey!
Well, let's put Oreld aside.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.370
I won't allow you to speak ill about Section III!

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.230
If you're going to apologize, great.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:31.760
If not, I'm going to do this move on you again!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:33.730
Why you...

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.200
Stekkin?!

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.710
It's embarrassing...

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.490
You little brat!

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:38.740
Pumpkin Scissor...s?
You little brat!

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.120
Pumpkin Scissor...s?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:42.990
Oreld!

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:45.210
See the power of my finishing move?

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:45.980
Shut up!

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:47.700
Hurry up and run already!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.150
Oh, this isn't good...

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:55.250
Come get us!

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:55.790
Shut up already!
Come get us!

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:56.800
Shut up already!

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.320
What're we going to do?

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:04.350
Isn't it obvious?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.270
Run.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:12.160
I don't want to get any scars on my face today, y'know.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.150
The corporal's been taken captive!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.400
He's really clumsy, isn't he?

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:22.660
This guy's recuperating from his injuries!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.770
Stop picking on weak people!

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:27.440
It's... escalating into something big...

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.030
Come on, place your bets!

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.010
Right now, Section III's odds are 16:1!

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:35.450
Lieutenant Webner?!

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:36.950
Hello there, Machs.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:38.420
Are you betting, as well?

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:40.350
What are you talking about?

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:42.590
Wait, what are you doing here?

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.470
Section I's chief called me up...

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.560
...about that tank incident.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.380
He asked me everything that I knew about it.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.120
Don't worry.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.900
I didn't mention anything about the big guy taking on the tank by himself.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.070
Actually, those people were more concerned about...

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.490
...those agents.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.910
Those agents?

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:08.930
Why now?

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:10.590
Beats me.

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.780
Anyway, if you call yourself a man...

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:15.560
...then get in there already!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.560
Yes, sir!

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:17.420
Well then-

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.670
You don't need to.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.370
But, but, but...

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.310
Time's up.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:25.680
Hey!

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.390
What the hell do you guys think you're doing?

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.890
Security?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.390
Restrain everyone!

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.990
Don't even think of moving!

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:34.730
And the match ends in a draw.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.660
The house takes everything.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:40.190
Machs jumped in for nothing.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:41.390
It's all good.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:42.320
It's punishment for him.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:45.430
He's been breaking too many of my cars lately.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:53.070
That Webner lady's pretty tough.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:56.760
She was formerly from the weapons department.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.600
Questioning her isn't an easy task.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:03.970
So, from her testimony just now,

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.860
what do you two think?

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:09.740
In relation to the waterworks incident?

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:10.900
Yes.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.600
This is my personal opinion,

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:16.480
but the rifles we seized from the waterworks staff...

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:21.000
...for automatic rifles, they are pretty complete.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:25.090
The ammunition's standards don't match those of Neburo's,

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:28.140
and when we test-fired three hundred rounds,

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.820
there was no jamming in the rifles at all.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.970
They are quite well standardized.

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:37.880
...while every other country is still using bolt-action rifles right now, eh?

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:41.080
If we have it order-made, we might be able to reproduce some,

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.960
but we wouldn't be able to maintain that quality for mass production.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.870
Yet here we have someone able to mass produce them at a high quality.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:52.210
This and the tank that Section III seized...

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:58.340
Indeed, it does connect with what Hunks told me.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.090
Those automatic rifles...

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.790
Could they be given to us?

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:07.540
In close combat situations,

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:11.860
the Republic's cylinders have an advantage over our rifles.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.750
Do not praise enemy technology.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:15.930
Then, even more-

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:24.120
Oh.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.940
So that's Alice L. Malvin,

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:30.510
the person that broke the double swords that you're so proud of?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.930
To think that she was that tiny of a figure...

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.260
There, you're all set.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:46.260
Sorry.

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:47.350
You should be more careful;

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:49.310
your injuries were almost healed.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:51.360
Sorry.

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.720
It seems like the mood's getting heavier.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:02.380
At this point, it looks as if I have no choice but to adopt Oreld-style ideas...

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.360
That last option...

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:05.380
That last option...

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:12.900
...is Plan C - "Comeback! The Amorous Sigh!"

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:13.680
Master Sergeant.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.080
Y-Yes?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:22.520
Umm... back in the cafeteria... about Sergeant Major Oreld...

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:28.130
I didn't have a clue at all...

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.010
...about how Sergeant Major Oreld felt...

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:37.260
I think about... nothing but myself...

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.720
I don't see what's going on around me...

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.920
And that's probably why...

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.800
I couldn't save him...

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.660
I screw up... get depressed...

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:00.240
I don't even notice it when everyone's trying to cheer me up...

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.160
...even though you all have your own worries, as well...

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.520
I think about nothing but myself...

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:20.790
Cheer up~ Cheer up and up~ Cheer up~

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:25.130
There's a delicious bowl of stew today~

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.880
Wipe your tears~

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.460
And eat up~

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:32.970
Let's eat~

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:37.770
A song from the Republic?

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:39.130
Surprised?

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.200
Isn't that enemy music?!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.340
If someone were to hear this-

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:49.900
Before I came to Section III, I was in the army band.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.970
I've loved music since I was a child,

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:55.950
and although I've sung many songs of the Empire,

00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:59.800
I actually love the songs of the Republic, as well.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.720
They didn't let me study them because they were enemy songs or whatever,

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:11.330
but I thought that if I came to S.S., I'd be able to study however much I wanted.

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:14.890
So, I tried very hard and got in.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:22.630
Everyone of us is here in Section III for their own important and hopeless reasons.

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:26.890
So it's completely okay for us to be selfish and think about ourselves.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:28.950
You should think more and more

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.980
and be who you think you should be.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:36.200
As your superior, that's what I think, Corporal.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:44.250
I don't really understand.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.600
Not yet...

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:50.230
But...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.210
I'll go apologize to Sergeant Major Oreld, at least.

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:59.590
That's the most important thing for me to do right now.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.810
Ah, and...

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:11.770
I liked that song...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.310
There's still space over here.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.180
It was today, huh?

00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:39.150
The last set of trucks that will bring the underground refugees to the state farm.

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:43.100
Well, now the state farms should be filled with people after this.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.460
Umm, Sergeant Major...

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:48.130
Oreld!

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:51.980
Hey, Marielle.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.070
I'm so glad!

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:55.040
Did you come to see us off?

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.950
Yes, because this is a new start for you, Marielle.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:03.350
This injury still hasn't healed?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.460
Ah, no.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.080
I got this from the cafeteria today.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:07.740
Right?

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.890
Y-Yes.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:17.360
Take care of your father.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.220
And they're gone now...

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.470
Hey, big guy.

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:48.200
Sorry about what I said back in the cafeteria.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.080
I just got irritated.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:55.790
The refugees that Section III "saved" and guided out were just one piece of the pie.

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:02.430
They just look at how many people we did or didn't save.

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.360
People aren't balls we throw in a basket.

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:09.290
If there are one thousand people and we only save one, is that a failure?

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:14.440
And do we tell that one person we saved "you were saved, but it's meaningless"?

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:20.380
Stuff like that was going through my head.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.490
But, whatever.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.160
But...

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.550
I want to save them all...

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:29.750
Is that right?

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:35.080
Then, we'll be getting into a fight in the near future again.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:38.880
Yes, sir.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:55.690
Since then, the corporal has been gradually cheering up again.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.000
Mine!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.410
Ah, you shouldn't do that!

00:20:58.410 --> 00:20:59.370
In the end, I wasn't able to do anything at all.
Ah, you shouldn't do that!

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:00.390
It's okay.
In the end, I wasn't able to do anything at all.

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.730
It's his fault for daydreaming.
In the end, I wasn't able to do anything at all.

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:02.440
It's his fault for daydreaming.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:07.450
If everyone's happy, that's fine!

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:15.790
But lately, Alice seems strange, too.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.130
I'm worried about her.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:23.080
God, Oreld.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:26.620
I let the great corporal take care of the manual labor.

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.430
I'm fine with that.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.980
Kiddo?

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.450
What's wrong?

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.050
You can't go in!

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:36.140
Why not?

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:39.590
Well... for the good of Section III's future...

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.900
...they're in the middle of a very important discussion...

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:47.600
Umm...

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:50.280
In other words...

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:54.910
As I said,

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.070
I will be wed.

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:34.230
Mer-kun, is Alice really going to get married?

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:36.050
There's a lovely ballroom party tonight,

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.900
but it seems like some evil plot is moving behind the scenes.

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:41.370
Next time, "A Sweet Trap."

00:23:41.370 --> 00:23:43.190
Come get us if you dare!
